@dwex
title: CV-05 - Convoyer survives a non-dislodging attack
desc:  Gilgamesch B.3.2.12 only dissolves the convoy if the fleet is
       actually dislodged. Here ENG attacks NTH unsupported, but NTH
       receives hold-support from MID (legal because a con order is not
       a movement order, B.3.1.2). NTH defends with strength 2, ENG
       attacks with strength 1, the attack should bounce, the convoy
       chain should stay intact and the army should arrive.

       KNOWN ENGINE LIMITATION: the corresponding test in
       test_convoy_examples.py is marked xfail. eval_k1's convoy-attacker
       dislodgement loop currently skips the strength comparison, so any
       nmove targeting a convoyer dislodges it. Fixing this needs the
       conflict to be resolved at the convoyer's field, not at the
       attacker's. The diagram below shows the INTENDED outcome.

map {
  Lon LCB 0, 0.0
  NTH O   2, 0.6
  Bel LC  4, 0.0
  ENG O   2,-0.6
  MID O   4, 0.6
  Lon --F NTH
  NTH --F Bel
  ENG --F NTH
  MID --F NTH
}

orders {
  En A Lon mve Bel
  En F NTH con Lon
  En F MID hsup NTH
  Ge F ENG mve NTH !
}
@end
